## Conventions

This project uses the leafcutter conventions:

- **Ticket-driven development**: all work starts in `tickets/00_inbox/`. Use `/build-feature <epic>` to drive an epic to completion.
- **Pre-commit hooks** via `commit_guardian`: run automatically on every `git commit`. Fix violations before committing — do not use `--no-verify`.
- **Skill-based agent prompting**: Claude Code reads `.claude/skills/<skill>/SKILL.md` for specialist guidance. Use `/glossary-bootstrap` once after install.
- **DECISION HISTORY blocks** in every modified Python file: each changed `.py` file must append a dated entry in the `# DECISION HISTORY` block at the file's end.

## Critical Rules

### Pre-commit Hooks
- Do NOT bypass hooks with `--no-verify` except for files this session did not touch.
- When `git commit` fails on pre-commit, invoke the `precommit-autofix` skill.

### Folder READMEs are load-bearing
Before editing any file in a gated folder (`.claude/agents/`, `.claude/skills/`,
`.claude/hooks/`, `alembic/versions/`), read the nearest-ancestor `README.md`.
The `readme_read_guard.py` hook will block edits if the README has not been read.
